wlcs v1.8.1: the text-input popup and child tests order the xdg_surface configure expectations after text_input.enter.

text_input_enters_grabbing_popup and text_input_enters_parent_surface_after_child_destroyed open with `InSequence seq;`,
so every EXPECT_CALL the test and its fixtures make afterwards joins one sequence. The fixtures' own expectations are
among them: XdgSurfaceStable, XdgToplevelStable and XdgPopupStable each expect `configure` any number of times, and they
are created after `EXPECT_CALL(text_input, enter(parent))`. A configure that arrives before that enter then violates
the sequence ("prerequisites are not satisfied"), though the test never says anything about configures.

xdg-shell lets a client map a window only after it acknowledged the initial configure, and keyboard focus (which the
text input follows, zwp_text_input_v3.enter) goes to a window when it maps, so every compositor that follows xdg-shell
sends that configure first; the same holds for the child toplevel. The text-input protocol states no order between the
two. What the tests are about is the order of the text input's enter and leave, so the sequence is now a named one and
only the text input's expectations are put in it. The expectations are unchanged.

Applied by scripts/wlcs.sh with `git apply`; drop it when wlcs fixes the tests upstream.

